    "&lt;p&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 14.98px;&quot;&gt;proposal is NOT therefore a lawful development.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The existing loft conversion by reason of the rear dormer not being fully within the rear roofslope, has not demonstrated that the materials used in the facing flank elevation of the rear dormer, when viewed from ground level, would appear to be of similar colour and design to the materials used in the main roof of the subject dwellinghouse. The existing development would not therefore be within the tolerances of Schedule 2, Part 1 Class B, Condition B.2 (a) of The Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended&lt;/p&gt;"
